From 7ebdd17db88f2591e26ffe7b047b817596423c57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SangamSitapuri07 <180774299+SangamSitapuri07@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:21:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add a read-only pickup schema version command

The owner's schema stayed at version 1 after a migration that printed the v1
and v2 success messages verbatim, because dist still held the older build. Log
wording could not distinguish an upgrade from a no-op, and my earlier reading of
that line as proof of the upgrade was wrong.

npm run pickups:version reports the recorded version and whether a migration is
still needed, without writing anything. It shares the migration's honest error
handling: an empty environment is named as such, known configuration failures
are classified, and no connection detail is printed.

The integration test asserts the command reports version 2 after migration, that
it says the schema is not migrated before that, that it never prints the
database URL, and that it explains a missing configuration. The README tells the
operator to run it when unsure and to rebuild dist if the printed text does not
match the documented wording.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
