From 0e7f7b875f140f6feeba79fac1be394adf8dade1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SangamSitapuri07 <180774299+SangamSitapuri07@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:30:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Show whether a catalog rate is in force yet

The catalog view claimed entries were 'not connected to pickup estimates',
which stopped being true when requests started pricing from the catalog. It now
says what actually happens: a request takes the newest rate already in force.

Each rate is also labelled 'in force' or 'not yet in force'. Rates must be
created with a future start, so a newly added rate is pending by design and
every pickup for that category returns NO_RATE until its start passes. The old
view showed only a timestamp, leaving the reader to work out why requests were
being rejected. The pending label says it outright.

Tests cover both directions: a 2099 start is labelled pending and mentions
NO_RATE, and a 2020 start is labelled in force without that warning.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
